      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{x\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y).$",
      "worked_solution": "Let the function $f(x,y)$ be defined as\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y).\n$$\n\nThe function $f(x,y)$ is continuous except when $4-x-y$  is negative or zero. However, at the point $(1,2)$,  the expression  $4-x-y$ is positive, so we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(1,2)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (1,2)}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-x-y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-1-2)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$",
